"persuade" is "cause to decide", where "decide" means "come to believe" or =
"come to intend". (IIRC, there is no good gismu for "intend".)
=20
> Solve one and maybe you will solve them all.

These mostly involve not an alternating pair but an alternating triple:

A: know that something is true
B: know how to do something
C: know to do something

A: find out that something is true
B: find out how to do something
C: -----

A: learn that something is true
B: learn (how) to do something
C: learn to do something

A: teach that something is true
B: teach (how) to do something
C: teach to do something

A: remember that something is true
B: remember how to do something
C: remember to do something

A: decide that something is true
B: decide how to do something
C: decide to do something

